      "E-learning is quickly becoming a part of everyday life, and it is likely that in the near future many people will study entirely online rather than walk into a classroom. When that day comes, our idea of \"going to school\" will change dramatically.",
      "On the bright side, learning will grow far more flexible and inclusive. We can foresee students attending live lectures from home, receiving AI-powered personalized tutoring, and running experiments in virtual laboratories, so quality education will reach even remote villages. Yet the picture will not be entirely rosy. Without face-to-face interaction, learners may feel isolated, self-discipline will matter more than ever, and the warm social life of campus, clubs, friendships and shared canteens, may gradually fade away.",
